(◕‿‿◕) pwnagotchi _version-build_status.
Hi! I'm a pwnagotchi fork by flippedgannet, please take good care of me!
Here are some basic things you need to know to raise me properly!
If you want to change my configuration, use /etc/pwnagotchi/config.toml
All the configuration options can be found on /etc/pwnagotchi/default.toml
but don't even try to change it; I will always rewrite it to original state!
If I suddenly refuse to work (ಥ﹏ಥ), try
~ pwnagotchi --debug

I'm managed by systemd. Here are some basic commands. (^◡◡^)
~ pwnylog (✜‿‿✜) - simple real-time log viewing
~ pwnystatus (#__#) - job status check
~ pwnykill (☓‿‿☓) - service restart in MANU mode
~ pwnyauto (⌐■_■) - return to AUTO mode

If you have a PiSugar battery or want to simplify the config process:
~ pwnygen (☼‿‿☼) - interactive wizard, run it as root: sudo pwnygen
  reads the current defaults from /etc/pwnagotchi/default.toml
  asks a few questions (name, iface, whitelist, AI, screen, web auth,
  watchdog blind-epoch limit, PiSugar, ...) and only then writes
  prompts before overwriting config.toml, nothing is written without a "y"
  every question has a [default: ...] hint, so plain Enter accepts it
  if a PiSugar is selected and not yet installed, bundled .deb packages
  from /usr/local/share/pwnagotchi/packages are installed offline
  (this step matters mainly because the PiSugar hardware revision can only
  be chosen interactively, via the debconf prompts shown during .deb setup)

Heads-up ( ≧◡≦)
After boot in AUTO mode I show a static boot splash while PyTorch and its
deps bootstrap in the background - no web UI until that's done. Slow SD
cards make it worse. Don't restart me, I'm not frozen.
Then the AI starts: epoch 1 is pure observation. By the end of it the
brain may go into inference or straight into learning, depending on what
it already knows. Both are normal, and can differ between boots.

Good luck with your training, and be careful! (♥‿‿♥)